Import "../../library/algebra/basis_reindexing.clean"
Import "../../library/logic/equivalence_operations.clean"
Source transport:
  Kind: other
  Label: Basis transport
  Title: Composition and reversal of basis reindexing

Text:
  Reindexing changes the labels of a basis. Applying e and then f uses the
  composite f after e; evaluating the resulting basis follows the inverse maps.

Result successive basis reindexing:
  Attribution: transport; composition law from Module.Basis.reindex_apply; adapted
  Let K,I,J,L: Type
  Let field: FieldStructure(K)
  Let M: CoefficientModule(K,field)
  Let b: ModuleBasis(K,field,M,I)
  Let e: Equivalence(I,J)
  Let f: Equivalence(J,L)
  Conclude:
    reindex module basis(field,M,reindex module basis(field,M,b,e),f) =
      reindex module basis(field,M,b,compose equivalences(e,f))

Result identity basis reindexing:
  Attribution: transport; identity law from Module.Basis.reindex_apply; adapted
  Let K,I: Type
  Let field: FieldStructure(K)
  Let M: CoefficientModule(K,field)
  Let b: ModuleBasis(K,field,M,I)
  Conclude: reindex module basis(field,M,b,identity equivalence(I)) = b

Result reversing basis reindexing:
  Attribution: transport; inverse law from Module.Basis.reindex_apply; adapted
  Let K,I,J: Type
  Let field: FieldStructure(K)
  Let M: CoefficientModule(K,field)
  Let b: ModuleBasis(K,field,M,I)
  Let e: Equivalence(I,J)
  Conclude:
    reindex module basis(field,M,reindex module basis(field,M,b,e),inverse equivalence(e)) = b

